// This is a commented line

/* 
  1. Program Structure
    a. Method creation - Defines the bounds of a method
      ```
      def METHOD_NAME::
        ...
      METHOD_NAME;
      ```

  2. Addressing References:
    - % is a program method name
    - @ is a global methiod name
    - * is a memory address pointer
    - $ is an memory address pointer relative to the application start
 
  3. Registers
    a. System Registers (Does not clear automatically)
      - PROGV - Program Variables Array
      - PC – Program Counter (Next address to be executed)
      - X0 – Always set to 0 when read (Is of the size of the memory width)
      - X1 – Return address
    b. Program Registers
      - S0 ... S07 - Static Interrupt Addresses
      - S8 - Program Interrupt Flag
      - S9 ... S15 - Program Interrupt Address
    b. Temporary Registers (Clears at every stack frame)
      - RP – Register Pointer
      - R0 ... R15 - Temp Registers
    c. ALU Registers (Math Registers)
      - AC – Accumulator
      - AR – Argument
    e. STACKV - Stack Variables
      - MV1 ... MV8
  
	R. Reference Tables
    a. Aliases
    	Register | Alias
    	---------|---------
    	X0       | ZERO
    	X1       | RA
    	X2       | SP
    	X3       | GP
	    X4 - X7  | T0 - T3
  	  X8 - X15 | P0 - P7
    	S0 - S7  | IR0 - IR7
	    S8       | SIRE
  	  S9 - S15 | SIR0 - SIR6
    	PC       | PC
    	A0			 | AC
    	A1       | AR
  	b. Datatypes
	    Datatype          | size in bytes
  	  ------------------|---------------
    	byte              | 1
	    unsigned byte     | 1 
  	  halfword          | 2
    	unsigned halfword | 2
	    word              | 4
  	  unsigned word     | 4
*/

def KEYBOARD_INTERRUPT::
  # SETR RP *R0
  @LDINTBUFF *R1
KEYBOARD_INTERRUPT;


def MAIN::
  SETR S8, *KEYBOARD_INTERRUPT;
MAIN;


def INIT::
  PROGV ERROR_CODE, 8
  SETI S0, %KEYBOARD_INTERRUPT;
  SETIB *R0,
  JMP %MAIN;
INIT;
